  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Camping Sunêlia L'Argentière is a 4-star campsite in Cogolin, in the heart of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez, 1.5 km from the town centre and 5 km from the beaches according to the tourist office. It has 248 pitches and 110 mobile homes (comfort, prestige and luxury ranges), a swimming pool and a restaurant.</p>

      <h2>Dogs at the campsite</h2>
      <p>The FAQ on the campsite's official website states: "Only small domestic animals (excluding exotic pets) are accepted (under 15 kg). Category 1 and 2 dogs are not accepted on the site." Animals must be supervised at all times and kept on a lead during the stay, with an up-to-date vaccination record; any safety breach can lead to the animal, its owner and companions being expelled. The Gulf of Saint-Tropez tourist office lists "pets accepted with a supplement"; the amount is not published on the pages consulted.</p>
      <p>The campsite is open from early April to late September or early October: the 2026 season ended on 27 September, and the 2027 season starts on 1 April (the campsite's website gives a closing date of 3 October 2027, the tourist office 30 September).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the campsite only accepts dogs under 15 kg. For a bigger dog this is not the right address: choose another place to stay around the gulf.</div>

      <h2>Les Marines de Cogolin beach</h2>
      <p>Municipal order no. 2026/634 (Les Marines beach rules, 2026 season) bans dogs from the beach, even on a lead, from 1am to 7pm between 15 June and 15 October 2026. From 7pm to 1am it is open to dogs on a lead, except 2nd-category dogs. Dogs remain banned from the swimming zone. The town hall also says a dog shower has been installed near the beach. This order applies to the 2026 season: re-read the following season's rules before you go.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Cogolin's harbour and the gulf's beaches round out a stay in the area nicely, as do <a href="/en/fiche-port-grimaud">Port Grimaud</a> and <a href="/en/fiche-sainte-maxime">Sainte-Maxime</a>, a few minutes away by car. On the spot, the <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-toutou-douche-cogolin">Cogolin dog wash</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-veterinaire-riviera-vet">Riviera Vet</a> practice in Sainte-Maxime are handy to keep in mind during your stay.</p>
